(Summary, written by PutiaCNC)
(Spindle (!):            Not run by the program: it stops -M0- to ask you to start it at the)
(                        speed shown, and again before a tool change and at the end to stop it.)
(                        There is no work coordinate system: jog to the zero of the job and set)
(                        it with G92 X0 Y0 Z0 first.)
(Tools:                  1/8in flat end mill, 6 mm flat end mill. No tool change.)
(Pauses:                 The program stops 6 times with the spindle off: 'Start the spindle at)
(                        12000 rpm, then resume', 'Stop the spindle . TEST 1: spindle off, tool)
(                        up . Press Resume', 'Start the spindle at 12000 rpm, then resume',)
(                        'Stop the spindle and change tool to 6 mm, then touch off Z 0 and)
(                        resume', 'Start the spindle at 12000 rpm, then resume', 'Stop the)
(                        spindle, then resume'. Resume it when you are ready; the spindle)
(                        starts again by itself.)
(Cutting:                Down to Z 7 mm. 1426 mm of cutting, about 2 min 17 s in all.)
(End:                    Lifts to Z 15 mm, goes to X0 Y0.)
(Air cut (!):            Operations 1, 2, 3 run 10 mm above the stock: nothing is cut.)
; PutiaCNC - Marlin (no spindle control)
; Stock 100 x 80 x 12 mm; XY0 = lower-left corner of stock, Z0 = top surface
